+| A3 | Narrowing §3(b) to a *duplicative permit-time* step does not let unreviewed code enforce spend or source restrictions; classification is by byte effect, not Executive label. | Deployed bytes on the exact dispatch path differ from the bytes whose control was independently verified, with no source-linked Economy/Judiciary record; or an Executive classifies an enacted control as a "formality" and dispatch continues. | Economy + Judiciary |
+| A4 | Removing a separate permit-time cap leaves the ordinary resource constraints genuinely binding and non-resettable. | Any office exceeds ordinary aggregate authority without fail-closed suspension, or the cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` ledger is reset by restart, rename, re-permitting or expansion. | Economy |
